109	//
110	//   version(1B) || set_id(4B, big-endian) || index(1B) || payload(32B) || checksum(4B)
111	//
112	// where `checksum` is the first 4 bytes of SHA-256 over the preceding 38 bytes. `set_id` ties the
113	// three shares of one split together; `combine_envelopes` refuses to combine shares whose `set_id`
114	// differs. The index is carried in the envelope, so a caller never has to track "which share is
